  researchPracticeReference:{id:'tesamorelin-egrifta-wr-label-reference',title:'Approved-label reference — EGRIFTA WR only',evidenceClass:'U.S. FDA approved-product labeling — HIV-associated lipodystrophy and formulation specific',transferable:false,amount:1.28,unit:'mg',stages:[{amount:1.28,unit:'mg',durationWeeks:null,schedule:{kind:'daily',days:[],times:['09:00'],interval:null}}],frequency:{kind:'daily',days:[],times:['09:00'],interval:null},durationWeeks:null,plannedBreakWeeks:null,defaultTime:'09:00',vialStrengthMg:11.6,diluentMl:1.3,provenance:{sourceIds:['FDA-EGRIFTA-WR-2025'],sourceUrls:['https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/022505s020lbl.pdf'],sourceTitle:'EGRIFTA WR (tesamorelin) U.S. Prescribing Information, revised March 2025',notes:'Approved-label context only for EGRIFTA WR in HIV-infected adults with lipodystrophy: 1.28 mg (0.16 mL) subcutaneously once daily after reconstituting the proprietary 11.6 mg vial with 1.3 mL of its supplied diluent. The label says EGRIFTA WR is not for weight-loss management and is not substitutable with EGRIFTA SV. These values are not a generic tesamorelin-vial recipe and do not transfer into Guide.'}},
  summary:'Tesamorelin has approved-product and randomized human evidence in a specific HIV-associated lipodystrophy context.',
  plainEnglish:'This evidence is stronger than for many research peptides, but indication, monitoring and product formulation matter. A research vial is not automatically interchangeable.',
